[TITLE]
Selection-ops fixture — SelectionOps::invert / SelectionOps::trace.

Topology (flow left to right):

    S1          S2 <- S3            S4
     |           |                   |
     v           v                   v
    J1 --C1--> J2 --C2--> J3 --C3--> O1
                           ^
                           |
                          P1 (pump)
                           |
                          J4  <- S4 drains here

  Nodes ....... J1 J2 J3 J4 (junctions), O1 (outfall)
  Links ....... C1 C2 C3 (conduits), P1 (pump, J4 -> J3)
  Subcatch .... S1 -> J1, S2 -> J2, S3 -> S2 (subcatchment outlet!), S4 -> J4
  Rain gage ... RG1

S3 -> S2 is the point of the fixture: it exercises subcatchment-to-subcatchment
outlet chaining in both trace directions. S4 hangs off the pump branch so a
downstream trace from S3 can be shown NOT to pick it up.

Category census (used by the invert tests): 4 junctions, 1 outfall, 3 conduits,
1 pump, 4 subcatchments, 1 rain gage = 14 objects.

[OPTIONS]
FLOW_UNITS       CFS
INFILTRATION     HORTON
FLOW_ROUTING     DYNWAVE
LINK_OFFSETS     DEPTH
MIN_SLOPE        0
START_DATE       01/01/2026
START_TIME       00:00:00
REPORT_START_DATE 01/01/2026
REPORT_START_TIME 00:00:00
END_DATE         01/01/2026
END_TIME         02:00:00
REPORT_STEP      00:01:00
ROUTING_STEP     00:00:30

